    # Verb Patterns: Gerund vs. Infinitive & Subtle Distinctions (76-130)
    ("I distinctly remember ______ the front door before getting into the taxi.", ["to lock", "locking", "lock", "locked"], 1, "'Remember + -ing' = pamatovat si na minulou vzpomínku (už jsem to udělal). ('Remember to do' = nezapomenout něco udělat).", "Remember DOING (vzpomínka) vs TO DO (úkol)."),
    ("Please remember ______ the alarm system before leaving the office tonight.", ["setting", "to set", "set", "having set"], 1, "'Remember + to infinitiv' = nezapomenout splnit budoucí úkol.", "Remember TO DO = nezapomeň udělat."),
    ("We regret ______ you that your application for the research grant was unsuccessful.", ["informing", "to inform", "inform", "informed"], 1, "Formální oznámení špatné zprávy: 'regret to inform / to say / to tell' (vždy infinitiv s 'to'!).", "Regret TO inform you (oznámení) vs regret DOING (lítost nad minulostí)."),
    ("She deeply regrets ______ down the internship in Zurich two years ago.", ["to turn", "turning", "turn", "turned"], 1, "Lítost nad minulým rozhodnutím: 'regret + -ing' (případně 'having turned').", "Regret DOING sth = litovat, že jsem to udělal."),
    ("If the screen freezes, try ______ the power button for ten seconds.", ["to hold", "holding", "hold", "held"], 1, "'Try + -ing' = vyzkoušet nějakou metodu/experiment, zda to pomůže. ('Try to do' = snažit se o něco obtížného).", "Try DOING (experiment) vs Try TO DO (snaha)."),
    ("Despite trying ______ the summit before sunset, the climbers had to set up camp early.", ["reaching", "to reach", "reach", "reached"], 1, "'Try + to infinitiv' = pokusit se / vynaložit snahu dosáhnout náročného cíle.", "Try TO DO = vynaložit úsilí."),
    ("After driving for four hours, we stopped ______ a quick espresso at a service station.", ["having", "to have", "have", "had"], 1, "'Stop + to infinitiv' = zastavit se za účelem (abychom si dali kávu).", "Stop TO DO (zastavit kvůli něčemu) vs Stop DOING (přestat s něčím)."),
    ("The factory had to stop ______ single-use plastic wrappers under the new law.", ["to produce", "producing", "produce", "produced"], 1, "'Stop + -ing' = přestat něco dělat / ukončit činnost.", "Stop DOING = přestat dělat."),
    ("Moving to Stockholm meant ______ to commute in sub-zero temperatures.", ["to learn", "learning", "learn", "learned"], 1, "'Mean + -ing' = obnášet / znamenat nutnost něčeho. ('Mean to do' = mít v úmyslu).", "Mean DOING (obnášet) vs Mean TO DO (mít v úmyslu)."),
    ("I didn't mean ______ your feelings; my remark was poorly phrased.", ["hurting", "to hurt", "hurt", "to hurting"], 1, "'Mean + to infinitiv' = mít v úmyslu / chtít.", "Didn't mean TO hurt you."),
    ("The director went on ______ the quarterly figures for another forty minutes.", ["to explain", "explaining", "explain", "explained"], 1, "'Go on + -ing' = pokračovat v téže činnosti dál. ('Go on to do' = přejít k dalšímu bodu).", "Go on DOING (pokračovat) vs Go on TO DO (přejít k novému tématu)."),
    ("After summarizing the budget, the CFO went on ______ the expansion strategy.", ["discussing", "to discuss", "discuss", "discussed"], 1, "'Go on + to infinitiv' = přejít k dalšímu tématu / kroku.", "Go on TO discuss = dále probrat."),
    ("I'll never forget ______ the Northern Lights above Tromsø for the first time.", ["to see", "seeing", "see", "seen"], 1, "'Never forget + -ing' = nezapomenout na silný minulý zážitek.", "Forget DOING (vzpomínka) vs Forget TO DO (zapomenout úkol)."),
    ("She forgot ______ the attachment before clicking 'Send' on the application email.", ["including", "to include", "include", "included"], 1, "'Forget + to infinitiv' = zapomenout něco udělat (úkol).", "Forgot TO include."),
    ("The ancient stonework urgently needs ______ before winter frost cracks the mortar.", ["to restore", "restoring", "restore", "restored"], 1, "Po 'need / want / require' s trpným významem u věcí následuje -ing (nebo to be V3): 'needs restoring'.", "Needs doing = needs to be done!"),
    ("Students are strongly advised ______ all coursework backups on cloud storage.", ["keeping", "to keep", "keep", "kept"], 1, "Po trpném rodě ('be advised / encouraged / warned') jde vždy infinitiv s 'to': 'advised to keep'.", "Advise doing (bez osoby) vs Advise sb TO DO (s osobou / v pasivu)!"),
    ("The airline recommends ______ at the terminal at least three hours prior to departure.", ["to arrive", "arriving", "arrive", "arrived"], 1, "Bez uvedené osoby po 'recommend / advise / allow / forbid' následuje gerundium (-ing)!", "Recommend DOING vs Recommend sb TO DO."),
    ("They don't allow ______ inside the botanical conservatory.", ["to smoke", "smoking", "smoke", "smoked"], 1, "Bez předmětu (osoby) po 'allow / permit' následuje gerundium: 'allow smoking'.", "Allow DOING vs Allow sb TO DO."),
    ("Visitors are not allowed ______ flash photography inside the cathedral.", ["taking", "to take", "take", "taken"], 1, "Když je v pasivu nebo s osobou, 'allow' bere infinitiv s 'to': 'allowed to take'.", "Be allowed TO do."),
    ("She dreads ______ to give an impromptu speech at next week's ceremony.", ["to have", "having", "have", "had"], 1, "Sloveso 'dread' (děsit se něčeho) se pojí s -ing: 'dreads having to...'. (Výjimka: idiom 'I dread to think').", "Dread + -ing."),
    ("He narrowly avoided ______ into a parked delivery van on the icy street.", ["to crash", "crashing", "crash", "crashed"], 1, "Po 'avoid' následuje VŽDY gerundium (-ing): 'avoided crashing'.", "Avoid + -ing (nikoli to do)."),
    ("The witness denied ______ any confidential documents from the archive.", ["to remove", "removing", "remove", "to removing"], 1, "Po 'deny' následuje VŽDY gerundium (-ing / having + V3).", "Deny + -ing."),
    ("I can't help ______ whether we overlooked an obvious clue in the transcript.", ["to wonder", "wondering", "wonder", "wondered"], 1, "Vazba 'can't help + -ing' = nemoci si pomoci / muset na něco myslet.", "Can't help + -ing."),
    ("It's no use ______ over a missed flight; let's check the next departure.", ["to panic", "panicking", "panic", "panicked"], 1, "Po 'It's no use / It's no good' následuje vždy gerundium (-ing).", "It's no use + -ing."),
    ("I'm really looking forward to ______ your research team in Vienna next month.", ["meet", "meeting", "met", "have meet"], 1, "Pozor! Ve frázi 'look forward to' je 'to' předložka ➔ následuje -ing ('meeting').", "Look forward TO + -ing!"),
    ("She isn't used to ______ so much administrative paperwork in her new role.", ["handle", "handling", "handled", "be handle"], 1, "'Be used to + -ing' = být zvyklý něco dělat (předložka 'to'!).", "Be/get used TO + -ing."),
    ("We used ______ every summer in a small wooden cabin near Brno.", ["spending", "to spend", "spend", "to spending"], 1, "'Used to + infinitiv' vyjadřuje minulý zvyk, který už netrvá ('used to spend').", "Used TO + V1 (minulý zvyk) vs Be used TO + -ing (být zvyklý)."),
    ("The defence lawyer objected to his client ______ questioned without counsel.", ["be", "being", "to be", "been"], 1, "'Object to' má předložku 'to' ➔ pasivní gerundium 'being questioned'.", "Object TO + -ing."),
    ("Would you mind ______ the projector slightly so everyone can see the slide?", ["to adjust", "adjusting", "adjust", "adjusted"], 1, "Po 'mind' následuje vždy gerundium (-ing): 'Would you mind adjusting...'.", "Mind + -ing."),
    ("The captain made the entire crew ______ the safety drill twice.", ["to repeat", "repeat", "repeating", "repeated"], 1, "Po činném 'make' a 'let' následuje holý infinitiv bez 'to': 'made the crew repeat'.", "Make sb DO sth (činný) vs Be made TO do sth (trpný)!"),
    ("Every new recruit was made ______ a strict non-disclosure agreement.", ["sign", "to sign", "signing", "signed"], 1, "V trpném rodě se u 'make' vrací 'to': 'was made to sign'.", "Was made TO do."),
    ("I watched the street artist ______ a portrait using only charcoal.", ["to draw", "draw", "to drawing", "drawn"], 1, "Po slovesech smyslového vnímání (watch/see/hear) pro celý děj následuje holý infinitiv ('draw') nebo -ing pro průběh.", "Watch sb DO / DOING sth."),
    ("They persuaded the reluctant landowner ______ a right-of-way across his pasture.", ["granting", "to grant", "grant", "granted"], 1, "Po 'persuade / convince / urge + osoba' následuje infinitiv s 'to'.", "Persuade sb TO do."),
    ("She suggested ______ a working lunch so we wouldn't fall behind schedule.", ["to have", "having", "have", "to having"], 1, "'Suggest' se NIKDY nepojí s infinitivem ('suggest to have' je chyba!). Správně: 'suggest having' nebo 'suggest that we have'.", "Suggest + -ing (nikoli suggest to do!)."),
    ("He admitted ______ the quarterly spreadsheet before submitting it to the board.", ["to alter", "to altering", "alter", "altered"], 1, "Po 'admit to' (přiznat se k) je 'to' předložka ➔ následuje -ing ('to altering').", "Admit TO + -ing."),
    ("I don't fancy ______ out in this freezing sleet; let's order soup instead.", ["to go", "going", "go", "gone"], 1, "Sloveso 'fancy' (mít chuť něco dělat) se pojí vždy s -ing: 'fancy going'.", "Fancy + -ing."),
